Takauji ASHIKAGA was a busho ( Japanese military commander ) from the late Kamakura period to the period of the Northern and Southern Courts ( Japan ) .
He was the first Seii Taishogun ( literally , `` great general who subdues the barbarians '' ) of the Muromachi bakufu ( Japanese feudal government headed by a shogun ) .
His real family name was Genji ( Minamoto clan ) .
He was born as the legitimate son of Sadachika ASHIKAGA , who was a distinguished family of Kawachi-Genji ( Minamoto clan ) .
At first , he was given a portion of his name from Takatoki HOJO , who was the regent , and called himself Takauji .
When Emperor Godaigo raised an army at Mt. <unk> in Hoki Province in Genko , he led the bakufu army as a powerful gokenin ( an immediate vassal of the shogunate in the Kamakura and Muromachi through Edo periods ) in the Kamakura bakufu ( Japanese feudal government headed by a shogun ) , but he raised an army in <unk> Shrine in Tanba Province and destroyed Rokuhara Tandai ( an administrative and judicial agency in Rokuhara , Kyoto ) .
He was regarded as the first achievement of the fall of the bakufu ( Japanese feudal government headed by a shogun ) , and he was given one character of his imina ( personal name ) of Emperor Godaigo 's imina ( personal name ) , and changed his name to Takauji .
While the Kenmu Restoration by Godaigo was gradually lost its support , he stayed in Kamakura and established his own political power in Kamakura after he suppressed the Nakasendai War .
Due to this , the relationship with the Imperial Court became worse , and he temporarily fled to Mt. Hiei due to Godaigo 's counterattack , but he escaped to Kyushu for a while .
He went to Kyoto again from Kyushu , and was appointed as Seii Taishogun by the retired Emperor Kogon and Emperor Komyo , and established a new samurai government ( the Muromachi bakufu [ Japanese feudal government headed by a shogun ] ) .
Godaigo moved to Yoshino and founded the Southern Court ( Japan ) .
After the establishment of the bakufu , he established two politics with his younger brother Tadayoshi ASHIKAGA , but later opposed Tadayoshi and developed into the Kanno Disturbance .
After the death of Tadayoshi , the war ended , but continued to suppress the <unk> forces such as the Southern Court and made efforts to stabilize the rule .
After the death of Emperor Godaigo ( died ) , Tenryu-ji Temple was built to pray for the soul of the dead .
Since he rose in revolt against Emperor Godaigo ( Emperor Godaigo ) , he was regarded as a rebel after the Meiji period , but after the Second World War , his personality changed greatly due to the change of historical view .
